WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:09.178
Welcome to Reds QGH Simulator. This narrated screen guide uses captures from the actual release. It explains the controls; it is not a live microphone recognition test.

00:00:09.433 --> 00:00:16.552
Choose Single Aircraft or Tactical, then check the procedure, tracks, aircraft profile, initial distance, speed and rate of turn.

00:00:16.802 --> 00:00:23.628
Check initial altitude and airfield settings. A runway designator is separate from runway orientation. Keep their units clear.

00:00:23.878 --> 00:00:31.230
In Normal QGH, turn right heading 230 assigns a right turn to the selected heading. The aircraft follows a curved path at its configured rate.

00:00:31.479 --> 00:00:38.060
In U/S Compass, use turn left now, turn right now, and stop turn now. Left and right work independently.

00:00:38.313 --> 00:00:45.790
Request a transmission to see the direction-finding indication. It follows the aircraft during the reply, holds briefly after release, then blanks.

00:00:46.046 --> 00:00:51.604
Watch the red acknowledgement and the highlighted control. The buttons remain available whenever you prefer manual control.

00:00:51.854 --> 00:00:57.935
Terminate the exercise to inspect the track and command history. Replay helps connect each instruction with the movement that followed.
